WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.642
SKiNN precalculates JAM for use in lensing applications.

00:00:04.722 --> 00:00:09.364
Formally,

00:00:09.444 --> 00:00:14.085
it is a function that maps an eight-dimensional
vector of galaxy parameters into a d by d image of vrms,

00:00:14.165 --> 00:00:18.807
the quadratic sum of velocity dispersion and
rotational velocity.

00:00:18.887 --> 00:00:23.529
The eight inputs describe a power-law elliptical
mass distribution and an elliptical Sérsic light profile,

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:28.251
plus the galaxy inclination and orbital anisotropy.

00:00:28.331 --> 00:00:32.973
The architecture consists of five blocks,

00:00:33.053 --> 00:00:37.695
each with two two-dimensional convolutional layers
followed by an upsampling layer and a ReLU nonlinearity,

00:00:37.775 --> 00:00:42.416
for about seven million trainable parameters.

00:00:42.496 --> 00:00:47.138
It is trained by minimizing a standard
mean-squared-error loss with the Adam optimizer,

00:00:47.218 --> 00:00:51.860
using a dataset generated by JAM through the GLEE
software so the network learns to mimic the JAM procedure.
